    "details": "<p><strong>About the Event:</strong></p>\n<p>Test your algorithmic trading and game theory skills in Pokerbots, a high-stakes algorithmic bot competition!</p>\n<p>Teams must code an autonomous Python bot to compete in a custom poker variant designed with modified Texas Hold&rsquo;em mechanics to prevent the use of public repositories.</p>\n<p><strong>Technical &amp; Runtime Constraints:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Environment: Python 3.11.</li>\n<li>Allowed Libraries: Standard Python libraries, <strong>NumPy</strong>, and <strong>SciPy</strong> only <em>(no <code dir=\"ltr\">pip</code> installations allowed at runtime)</em>.</li>\n<li>Compute Limits: 1 vCPU, 1 GB RAM, read-only filesystem, and <strong>zero network access</strong>.</li>\n<li>Time Bank: Cumulative time bank per match (~60 seconds for 400 hands) with a hard wall-clock kill. Crashes or exhausted time banks result in match forfeiture.</li>\n<li>Communication Protocol: Bots operate automatically via a predefined stdin/stdout protocol.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Tournament Structure &amp; Progression:</strong></p>\n<p>All matches utilize <strong>duplicate deals</strong> (playing every deal twice with swapped seats) to mitigate luck and seat advantage.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Stage 1 (Swiss Qualifier): Valid bots play 6 rounds of ~200 duplicate deals (400 hands). Match points: <strong>1 for Win, 0.5 for Draw, 0 for Loss</strong>.</li>\n<li>Stage 2 (Top 32 Finals): The top 32 qualifying teams advance to a full round-robin stage (~500 duplicate deals each). Scores reset prior to this stage.</li>\n<li>Tie-Breakers: Calculated using a capped chips per hand formula.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rules &amp; Regulations:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Team Size: Teams must consist of <strong>exactly 2 members</strong>. An individual can only be on one team.</li>\n<li>Submissions: Teams can re-upload/overwrite submissions until <strong>November 15th at 23:59 IST</strong>. Only the last valid upload counts.</li>\n<li>Fair Play &amp; Code Review: Code copying, collusion, and network calls are strictly prohibited. Winners' source code will undergo a thorough manual review prior to prize payouts.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Evaluation Criteria:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Duplicate Deal Performance: Match points accrued during the Swiss Qualifier and final standings in the round-robin stage.</li>\n</ul>",
    "end_date": "2026-11-12T23:59:00+05:30",
